note The close icon in a panel's header closes that panel: its neighbour in the split takes the whole of the split's room. The reader reaches for it to get the room of a panel back; without it a split could never be undone. The views it held are hidden until picked again or revealed by navigation. The button is not shown when one panel fills the window.

